#: ../../../dev/building.rst:4
msgid "Building Syncthing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:7
msgid ""
"You probably only need to go through the build process if you are going to "
"do development on Syncthing or if you need to do a special packaging of it. "
"For all other purposes we recommend using the official binary releases "
"instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:12
msgid ""
"If you still prefer to build Syncthing from source for your own use, be "
"aware that there is a built-in automatic upgrade mechanism that will "
"overwrite your built binary with a downloaded version. To avoid this, you "
"can use the ``--no-upgrade`` build flag (see below), but you will be "
"responsible for your own upgrades."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:19
msgid "Branches and Tags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:21
msgid ""
"You should base your work on the ``main`` branch when doing your "
"development. This branch is usually what will be going into the next release "
"and always what pull requests should be based on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:25
msgid ""
"If you're looking to build and package a release of Syncthing you should "
"instead use the latest tag (``vX.Y.Z``) as the contents of ``main`` may be "
"unstable and unsuitable for general consumption."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:30
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:32
msgid ""
"The latest stable version of Go. The previous stable version should also "
"work; older versions will likely not work. This largely follows Go's "
"`Release Policy <https://go.dev/doc/devel/release#policy>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:36
msgid ""
"Usually, a C compiler. Syncthing uses SQLite for storing data and the most "
"common implementation is written in C."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:41
msgid ""
"Don't skip the C compiler, and make sure to build syncthing with "
"``CGO_ENABLED=1`` if you are cross compiling. While the build will succeed "
"with ``CGO_ENABLED=0`` and the resulting binary will work, it will run with "
"significantly lower performance and higher memory usage when the C "
"implementation of SQLite couldn't be used. Your users will not thank you."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:47
msgid ""
"Git, unless you're building from a downloaded source tarball that includes a "
"``RELEASE`` marker with the version information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:50
msgid ""
"If you want to build Debian packages FPM is required. See FPM's "
"`installation information <https://fpm.readthedocs.io/en/latest/installation."
"html>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:53
msgid ""
"To build Windows executables, installing `goversioninfo <https://github.com/"
"josephspurrier/goversioninfo>`__ is recommended in order to add file "
"properties and icon to the compiled binaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:57
msgid ""
"Building Android binaries requires `Android NDK <https://developer.android."
"com/ndk>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:59
msgid ""
"If you're not already a Go developer, the easiest way to get going is to "
"download the latest version of Go as instructed in https://go.dev/doc/"
"install."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:64
msgid "Building (Unix)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:66 ../../../dev/building.rst:91
msgid "Install the prerequisites."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:67
msgid "Open a terminal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:68 ../../../dev/building.rst:93
msgid "Run the commands below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:70
msgid ""
"# Pick a place for your Syncthing source.\n"
"$ mkdir -p ~/dev\n"
"$ cd ~/dev\n"
"\n"
"# Grab the code.\n"
"$ git clone https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing.git\n"
"\n"
"# Now we have the source. Time to build!\n"
"$ cd syncthing\n"
"\n"
"# You should be inside ~/dev/syncthing right now.\n"
"$ go run build.go"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:85
msgid ""
"Unless something goes wrong, you will have a ``syncthing`` binary built and "
"ready in ``~/dev/syncthing/bin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:89
msgid "Building (Windows)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:92
msgid "Open a ``cmd`` Window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:95
msgid ""
"# Pick a place for your Syncthing source.\n"
"> md \"%USERPROFILE%\\dev\"\n"
"> cd /d \"%USERPROFILE%\\dev\"\n"
"\n"
"# Grab the code.\n"
"> git clone https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing.git\n"
"\n"
"# Now we have the source. Time to build!\n"
"> cd syncthing\n"
"> go run build.go"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:108
msgid ""
"Unless something goes wrong, you will have a ``syncthing.exe`` binary built "
"and ready in ``%USERPROFILE%\\dev\\syncthing\\bin``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:112
msgid "Subcommands and Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:114
msgid "The following ``build.go`` subcommands and options exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:116
msgid "``go run build.go install``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:117
msgid ""
"Installs binaries in ``./bin`` (default command, this is what happens when "
"build.go is run without any commands or parameters)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:120
msgid "``go run build.go build``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:121
msgid ""
"Builds just the named target, or ``syncthing`` by default, to the current "
"directory. Use this when cross compiling, with parameters for what to cross "
"compile to: ``go run build.go --goos linux --goarch 386 build``. When cross "
"compiling you need to have a C compiler for the target platform, and you "
"need to let Go know how to invoke it. The ``--cc`` flag to build.go controls "
"this, together with the environment variable ``CGO_ENABLED=1``. For example, "
"to cross build from Linux to Windows using Zig as the C compiler, ``go run "
"build.go -goos windows -goarch amd64 -cc \"zig cc -target x86_64-windows\" "
"build``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:131
msgid "``go run build.go test``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:132
msgid "Runs the tests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:134
msgid "``go run build.go deb``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:135
msgid ""
"Creates a Debian package in the current directory. Requires FPM and a Unixy "
"build."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:138
msgid "``go run build.go tar``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:139
msgid ""
"Creates a Syncthing tar.gz dist file in the current directory. Assumes a "
"Unixy build. Otherwise same considerations and parameters as for the "
"``build`` subcommand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:143
msgid "``go run build.go zip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:144
msgid ""
"Creates a Syncthing zip dist file in the current directory. Assumes a "
"Windows build. Otherwise same considerations and parameters as for the "
"``build`` subcommand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:148
msgid ""
"The options ``--no-upgrade``, ``--goos`` and ``--goarch`` can be given to "
"influence ``build``, ``tar`` and ``zip``. Examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:151
msgid "``go run build.go --goos linux --goarch 386 tar``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:152
msgid "Builds a tar.gz distribution of Syncthing for linux-386."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:154
msgid "``go run build.go --goos windows --no-upgrade zip``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:155
msgid ""
"Builds a zip distribution of Syncthing for Windows (current architecture) "
"with upgrading disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:160
msgid ""
"Cross compiling with C (``CGO_ENABLED=1``) can be non-trivial; nonetheless "
"you should try to do so when at all possible. We use Zig to ease the pain; "
"you can check our `build workflows <https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing/"
"blob/main/.github/workflows/build-syncthing.yaml>`__ for inspiration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:169
msgid "Version Tagging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:171
msgid ""
"The binaries are \"tagged\" with a version derived from the current Git "
"commit, the most recent Git tag, and the current username and hostname. The "
"Git commit and tag can be replaced by a ``RELEASE`` file; see below. The "
"username and hostname can be overridden by the ``BUILD_USER`` and "
"``BUILD_HOST`` environment variables, for example::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:177
msgid ""
"$ BUILD_USER=builder BUILD_HOST=buildhost.local go run build.go\n"
"$ ./bin/syncthing --version\n"
"syncthing v1.8.0 ... builder@buildhost.local 2020-07-30 11:49:14 UTC"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:181
msgid ""
"In addition the timestamp (by default taken from the current Git commit) can "
"be overridden by the ``SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH`` variable, in Unix epoch seconds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:185
msgid ""
"If your built binary fails with an ``Invalid version string`` error, you "
"probably did not fetch the Git tags with the code. This can happen when "
"forking the repository on GitHub if you select the option to \"Copy the "
"``main`` branch only\". To fetch the tags on a fork, run these commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:190
msgid ""
"# Add the upstream repository as a remote\n"
"$ git remote add upstream https://github.com/syncthing/syncthing.git\n"
"\n"
"# Fetch all tags from the upstream remote\n"
"$ git fetch --tags upstream\n"
"\n"
"# Rebuild\n"
"$ go run build.go"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:203
msgid "Building without Git"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:205
msgid ""
"Syncthing can be built perfectly fine from a source tarball of course. If "
"the tarball is from our build server it contains a file called ``RELEASE`` "
"that informs the build system of the version being built. If you're building "
"from a different source package, for example one automatically generated by "
"GitHub, you must instead pass the ``--version`` flag to ``build.go``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:212
msgid ""
"If you are building something that will be installed as a package (Debian, "
"RPM, ...) you almost certainly want to use ``--no-upgrade`` as well to "
"prevent the built in upgrade system from being activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:216
msgid "``go run build.go --version v0.10.26 --no-upgrade tar``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../dev/building.rst:217
msgid ""
"Builds a tar.gz distribution of Syncthing for the current OS/arch, tagged as "
"``v0.10.26``, with upgrades disabled."
msgstr ""
